stubs passed to the hook.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T9"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.534,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"call `pytest_collection_modifyitems` with a fake item under tests/scripts/test_vartmp_cap.py\"","No description of the fake's attributes, or of the session/config arguments passed to the hook."],"finding":"The plan says to call `pytest_collection_modifyitems` with 'a fake item' but does not say what the fake item, session and config must provide for the glue to run. Unstated details include:\n- which path attribute the item exposes (`item.path` vs `item.fspath`);\n- whether that path is absolute under the real repo root, so the repo-relative computation resolves to `tests/scripts/test_vartmp_cap.py`;\n- how `add_marker` calls are recorded;\n- what is passed for `session`/`config`, given the hook may run other logic such as the collection isolation guard.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f108e930063d20ab1","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach","norm_id":"nc2836644751fc686","priority":0.066,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["If the fake path is relative or resolved against a different root, the relative-path computation does not match, and the win32 case fails for a test-construction reason rather than a glue defect.","If other logic in the hook dereferences config/session, a bare None or stub crashes the test."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Build the fake item's path as REPO_ROOT / 'tests/scripts/test_vartmp_cap.py', using the same repo-root the loaded conftest uses. Record add_marker arguments in a list. Pass minimal stubs (or the real `pytestconfig`) for session/config, consistent with how test_collection_isolation_guard.py drives the hook.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reword the AC to require that the win32 case fails when the `_linux_host_script_skip_reason` call is removed from the hook, and record the failing pytest output on the ticket/change.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T9"],"criteria":["E6","F1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.5371,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"by showing one fails when the glue call is removed\""],"finding":"The mutation check says 'showing one fails when the glue call is removed' without naming which case must fail. It should be the win32 case; the linux case would still pass. The plan also does not say where the result of this one-off check is recorded, so the evidence is not durable after the session.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0ff29b54c81dc173","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"n32ae7046998d04bd","priority":0.0629,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer cannot tell whether the RED check was actually done, or whether it was the meaningful case."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"AC: 'With the glue call temporarily removed, `pytest tests/unit/test_conftest_windows_skip_rule.py -k win32` fails (output pasted on the change). With it restored, both cases pass.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that `sys.platform` is patched with pytest's `monkeypatch.setattr(sys, 'platform', ...)` so it is restored automatically after each case.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T9"],"criteria":["T9","E2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.5175,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"`sys.platform` patched to win32\"","\"repeat with linux\""],"finding":"The plan patches the process-global `sys.platform` to win32/linux but does not say how the patch is undone, for example via `monkeypatch.setattr`. A leaked patch can affect later tests in the same process.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f99effb81ffc47ccd","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach","norm_id":"n789d55089ef286b9","priority":0.0825,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A manual assignment that is not restored makes later tests in the session